  "problem": "${lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n/3}=$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall the following special limit: \n\n$$\ne={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the given limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n/3} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{[{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}]}^{1/3} \\\\  & ={[{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}]}^{1/3} \\\\  & ={e}^{1/3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{e}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
